# 12-1 Momentum Metric

The 12-1 momentum metric is the standard measure for price momentum in quantitative investing.

## Formula

```
Momentum = (Price today / Price 12 months ago) - (Price today / Price 1 month ago)
```

## Implementation

1. Calculate 12-month return (excluding most recent month)
2. Rank all stocks by this metric
3. Buy top decile (or top 20%)
4. Hold for 3-6 months
5. Rebalance monthly

The exclusion of the most recent month avoids short-term reversals that would distort the signal.

